nt amoxicillin use suggest chronic rather than acute pathology", "Isolated Cardiac Syndrome: Tricuspid stenosis alone doesn't explain the respiratory features, but remains a possible comorbidity"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic multisystem respiratory involvement (sinuses + airways)", "Congenital tricuspid stenosis", "Growth parameters consistent since birth (suggesting systemic involvement)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis and Related Genetic Airway Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3128115491681232, "posterior": 0.3611952585117106, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Lack of documented immune findings weakly supports CF (B1) and chronic infections (B2) over primary immunodeficiency (B3), which requires specific immunologic …"], "evidence_against": ["The subacute presentation and normal growth parameters slightly reduce the probability of chronic infections (B2) and other constitutional disorders, but the e…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Lower Respiratory Tract Infections", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.09, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The subacute presentation and normal growth parameters slightly reduce the probability of chronic infections (B2) and other constitutional disorders, but the e…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Primary Immunodeficiency with Airway Involvement", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.011, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["MRI findings of airway dilation argue against bacterial bronchitis (B2.1) as the sole cause but do not directly affect CFTR-related disorders (B1.1.1, B1.1.2)."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Other Constitutional or Systemic Disorders", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.02, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis (CFTR-Related Mutation)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.26102155758399687, "posterior": 0.3227702310104648, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic productive cough and sinus symptoms since birth moderately support CFTR-related disorders due to their characteristic airway hypersecretion and sinus i…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of definitive sweat chloride testing weakens but doesn't exclude cystic fibrosis, maintaining it as a probable but unconfirmed diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1.1", "B1.1.2", "B1.1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia (PCD) with Airway Dysfunction", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of situs inversus and ciliary ultrastructural abnormalities moderately reduces the likelihood of primary ciliary dyskinesia."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Other Rare Genetic Airway Disorders (e.g., Mucopolysaccharidoses)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.019, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Recurrent Bacterial Bronchitis", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.034, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_again