resentation)\n    (frequency: frequent)\n    Suggestion: Evaluate for bronchiectasis and assess for chronic mucus hypersecretion via imaging or pulmonary function testing to support atypical CFTR diagnosis\n  repeated respiratory infections with amoxicillin treatment → recurrent respiratory tract infections due to impaired mucociliary clearance → Classic Cystic Fibrosis with Elevated Sweat Chloride\n    (frequency: obligate)\n    Suggestion: Investigate for CFTR dysfunction despite normal bowel movements, including sweat chloride testing and nasal potential difference analysis\n  height/weight in 25th percentile since birth → constitutional growth delay with chronic disease impact → Primary Immunodeficiency with Airway Involvement\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Assess for underlying immune deficiency through immunoglobulin levels and lymphocyte subset analysis\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
